The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
ret = __nvme_submit_sync_cmd(ctrl->connect_q, &cmd, &res, data, sizeof(*data), qid, NVME_SUBMIT_AT_HEAD | NVME_SUBMIT_RESERVED | NVME_SUBMIT_NOWAIT);
if (ret) {
    nvmf_log_connect_error(ctrl, ret, le32_to_cpu(res.u32), &cmd, data);
}
```
Reason:
When the I/O command connection fails (indicated by a non-zero `ret`), the error is logged, but the function continues to execute and attempts authentication, which overrides the original error captured from the connection attempt. This results in incorrect return values and improper error handling.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
+		goto out_free_data;
```
Reason:
By adding the `goto out_free_data;` statement after logging the connection error, the function is instructed to skip the subsequent authentication attempts and directly proceed to clean up and return the original error. This ensures that the error from the connection attempt is preserved and returned correctly.

